  "topic": "trees",
  "difficulty": "Medium",
  "pattern": "trees / Path accumulate",
  "statement": "# Root-to-Leaf Numbers\n\nThe tree is given as a level-order array `root`: the children of the entry at index `i` live at indices `2i+1` (left) and `2i+2` (right). An entry holding `null` means that child is absent and is skipped while traversing.\n\nEvery present node holds a single decimal digit (`0` to `9`). Each root-to-leaf path spells a decimal number: starting from `0` at the root's parent, each step updates `value = value * 10 + digit`. A lone root is itself a leaf, contributing its own digit.\n\nReturn the sum of the numbers spelled by all root-to-leaf paths.\n\nConstraints: `1 <= root.length <= 30`, `0 <= root[i] <= 9`, and `root[0]` is present.\n",
  "examples": [
    {
      "input": "root = [1,2,3]",
      "output": "25",
      "explanation": "The paths spell 12 and 13, which sum to 25."
    },
    {
      "input": "root = [4,9,0,5,1]",
      "output": "1026",
      "explanation": "The paths spell 495, 491, and 40; together they total 1026."
    },
    {
      "input": "root = [1,0]",
      "output": "10",
      "explanation": "A single zero child still extends the path, spelling 10."
    }
  ],
  "constraints": [
    "Function signature: `function sumNumbers(root: number[])`.",
    "Inputs are JSON-serializable values satisfying the bounds stated above."
  ],
  "hints": [
    "Carry the prefix number downward, not upward.",
    "Each step multiplies the prefix by 10 before adding the digit.",
    "Add to the total only at leaves \u2014 nodes with no present children."
  ],
  "editorial": {
    "approach": "Depth-first walk carrying the number built so far; each step multiplies by ten and adds the digit, adding the total at every leaf.",
    "why_optimal": "Each node is visited once with constant extra work, so time is linear and stack space follows the height. On 28 PAF-verified cases the judge measured the brute force at 0.46 ms and the optimal at 0.16 ms (about 2.9x faster).",
    "pitfalls": "Zeros are real digits that shift place values; a missing child ends a path but a zero child extends it."
  },
